# Context7 Documentation Checks

- Before writing or changing code that depends on external libraries, frameworks, SDKs, APIs, CLIs, or platform features, check the official docs using Context7 first.
- Prefer Context7 results over memory when there is any uncertainty about API behavior, options, signatures, config, or version-specific changes.
- Base implementation details on what Context7 confirms.
- If documentation cannot be found in Context7, state that clearly and ask the user whether to proceed with best-effort assumptions.
- Keep this process lightweight: only fetch the docs needed for the current task.
